raw_content:
Now update chars.js: templates carry hFrac; matchSegment takes optional lineHEst (or segHFrac). Implement two-pass:

- templates(): include hFrac: t.h.
- matchSegment(grid, segAspect, segHFrac): score += 1.0 × max(0, |segHFrac − t.hFrac| − 0.06) when segHFrac provided.
- In segmentAndRecognize/fallbackSegment, first pass: matchSegment(grid, aspect) without hFrac (pass segHFrac=undefined → skip term).
- After segmentation in recognizeChars: compute advanceEst = (last.x1 - first.x0 + 1)/nSeg... better pitch = mean of consecutive x0 diffs? With 4-5 segs, span/n fine. lineH = advanceEst × LINE_OVER_ADVANCE. Then for each seg: recompute grid (need y0/y1 — store them in seg objects) and re-match with segHFrac = segH/lineH. Update ch/conf/cost.

Store y0,y1 in seg objects. Then re-score pass.

Careful: re-scoring may change DP-chosen char; that's the point.

Implementation details: in segmentAndRecognize, segScore entries need y0,y1. Add. In recognizeChars after segs obtained:

```
const span = segs[segs.length-1].x1 - segs[0].x0 + 1;
const advanceEst = span / segs.length;
const lineH = advanceEst * LINE_OVER_ADVANCE;
for (const s of segs) {
  const grid = normalizeRegion(gray, width, height, s.x0, s.y0, s.x1, s.y1);
  const m = matchSegment(grid, (s.x1-s.x0+1)/(s.y1-s.y0+1), (s.y1-s.y0+1)/lineH);
  s.ch = m.best.ch; s.cost = m.best.score; s.conf = ...;
}
```

But wPen lost — fine for re-score.

Also update matchSegment signature: (grid, segAspect, segHFrac=null).

